 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "P01",
   "who": "penny",
   "text": "How does a company... end up running a country?"
  },
  {
   "id": "P02",
   "who": "stampy",
   "text": "Paperwork."
  },
  {
   "id": "P03",
   "who": "atlas",
   "text": "Bengal, seventeen fifty-seven. The richest province in all of Mughal India."
  },
  {
   "id": "P04",
   "who": "pike",
   "text": "Why is there always a river?!"
  },
  {
   "id": "P05",
   "who": "quill",
   "text": "The Nawab took Calcutta in seventeen fifty-six. Robert Clive took it back in January seventeen fifty-seven."
  },
  {
   "id": "P06",
   "who": "penny",
   "text": "Which brings us to... business."
  },
  {
   "id": "P07",
   "who": "stampy",
   "text": "A secret agreement! Help us win, and you become Nawab. Sign here... and here... and here..."
  },
  {
   "id": "P08",
   "who": "atlas",
   "text": "Twenty-third of June, seventeen fifty-seven. Plassey. The Company is massively outnumbered."
  },
  {
   "id": "P09",
   "who": "pike",
   "text": "Rule one of battles: keep your powder dry. Rule two: I am also wet."
  },
  {
   "id": "P10",
   "who": "quill",
   "text": "And the Nawab's own commander? He... just didn't fight."
  },
  {
   "id": "P11",
   "who": "penny",
   "text": "New ruler. Same throne. Different owner."
  },
  {
   "id": "P12",
   "who": "quill",
   "text": "Actually, that's just Bengal. The rest took another hundred years."
  }
 ]
}